    "requirement_statement": {
      "text": "",
      "statements": [
        {
          "modal": "Must",
          "text": "When a record is satisfied in more than one location (prompt, skill,\nagent, template or code), judge-jev MUST judge the record separately at\neach location."
        },
        {
          "modal": "Must",
          "text": "judge-jev MUST report one result per (record, location) pair."
        },
        {
          "modal": "MustNot",
          "text": "judge-jev MUST NOT combine a record's locations into one judgment."
        }
      ]
    },
    "rationale": "Rand (2026-11-07): \"from raptor config standpoint for judge-jev, we must\nhave single requirements mapped to multiple places in\nprompts/skills/agents/code I would expect a separate jev query for each\nlocation it is satisfied. We may be able to fan out a single jev call w/\n<location> - <question-1-req-1> | <question-2-req-1> | <question-3-req-2>\n| <question-4-req-2> | ... depending on how we can fit items in context\"\nRand (2026-11-08): \"batching is simply streaming of single requests.\"",
    "success_criteria": {
